{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"e16e0d676bbefde52e47cf45","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560%40gmail.com/","channels":["linux-i2c"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560%40gmail.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com"},"subject":"[PATCH] i2c: mxs: fix DMA channel leak on probe error","messages":{"20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com":{"id":"20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com","messageId":"20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com","references":[],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Ruoyu Wang","address":"ruoyuw560@gmail.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"Shawn Guo","address":"shawnguo@kernel.org"},{"name":"Sascha Hauer","address":"s.hauer@pengutronix.de"},{"name":"Pengutronix Kernel Team","address":"kernel@pengutronix.de"},{"name":"Fabio Estevam","address":"festevam@gmail.com"},{"name":"Marek Vasut","address":"marex@denx.de"},{"name":"Wolfram Sang","address":"wsa@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"imx@lists.linux.dev"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"Ruoyu Wang","address":"ruoyuw560@gmail.com"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-14T13:40:33.000Z","iso":"2026-08-14T13:40:33.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"[PATCH] i2c: mxs: fix DMA channel leak on probe error","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"dma_request_chan() grants the driver exclusive use of the channel until\ndma_release_channel() is called. If controller reset or I2C adapter\nregistration fails after the request, mxs_i2c_probe() returns without\nreleasing it. The failed probe does not invoke mxs_i2c_remove(), so the\nchannel remains allocated and can prevent a later probe from acquiring\nit."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Release the DMA channel on both post-request error paths. Keep the\nadapter-registration unwind ordered after the existing controller reset."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"This issue was found by a static analysis checker and confirmed by\nmanual source review."},{"kind":"code","text":"Fixes: 62885f59a261 (\"MXS: Implement DMA support into mxs-i2c\")"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Signed-off-by: Ruoyu Wang <ruoyuw560@gmail.com>"},{"kind":"patch","patchId":"patch:20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com:0:0"}],"patchIds":["patch:20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com:0:0"],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[]},"an8ntm6GRhFJnrqZ@SMW015318":{"id":"an8ntm6GRhFJnrqZ@SMW015318","messageId":"an8ntm6GRhFJnrqZ@SMW015318","references":["20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com"],"missingAncestorIds":[],"author":{"name":"Frank Li","address":"Frank.li@oss.nxp.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Ruoyu Wang","address":"ruoyuw560@gmail.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"Andi Shyti","address":"andi.shyti@kernel.org"},{"name":"Shawn Guo","address":"shawnguo@kernel.org"},{"name":"Sascha Hauer","address":"s.hauer@pengutronix.de"},{"name":"Pengutronix Kernel Team","address":"kernel@pengutronix.de"},{"name":"Fabio Estevam","address":"festevam@gmail.com"},{"name":"Marek Vasut","address":"marex@denx.de"},{"name":"Wolfram Sang","address":"wsa@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-i2c@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"imx@lists.linux.dev"},{"name":"","address":"linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-14T14:35:34.000Z","iso":"2026-08-14T14:35:34.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH] i2c: mxs: fix DMA channel leak on probe error","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-i2c.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"quote","attribution":"On Fri, Aug 14, 2026 at 09:40:33PM +0800, Ruoyu Wang wrote:","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"[You don't often get email from ruoyuw560@gmail.com. Learn why this is important at https://aka.ms/LearnAboutSenderIdentification ]"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"dma_request_chan() grants the driver exclusive use of the channel until"},{"depth":1,"text":"dma_release_channel() is called. If controller reset or I2C adapter"},{"depth":1,"text":"registration fails after the request, mxs_i2c_probe() returns without"},{"depth":1,"text":"releasing it. The failed probe does not invoke mxs_i2c_remove(), so the"},{"depth":1,"text":"channel remains allocated and can prevent a later probe from acquiring"},{"depth":1,"text":"it."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Release the DMA channel on both post-request error paths. Keep the"},{"depth":1,"text":"adapter-registration unwind ordered after the existing controller reset."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"This issue was found by a static analysis checker and confirmed by"},{"depth":1,"text":"manual source review."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Fixes: 62885f59a261 (\"MXS: Implement DMA support into mxs-i2c\")"},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Ruoyu Wang <ruoyuw560@gmail.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":" drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mxs.c | 5 ++++-"},{"depth":1,"text":" 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mxs.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mxs.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 4e07babea9c3f..a5c8b44ec8142 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mxs.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mxs.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -849,8 +849,10 @@ static int mxs_i2c_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"        /* Do reset to enforce correct startup after pinmuxing */"},{"depth":1,"text":"        err = mxs_i2c_reset(i2c);"},{"depth":1,"text":"-       if (err)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+       if (err) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+               dma_release_channel(i2c->dmach);"}],"lineCount":32,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Please use devm_dma_request_chan() to fix this problem"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Frank"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"                return err;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+       }"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"        adap = &i2c->adapter;"},{"depth":1,"text":"        strscpy(adap->name, \"MXS I2C adapter\", sizeof(adap->name));"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -865,6 +867,7 @@ static int mxs_i2c_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)"},{"depth":1,"text":"        if (err) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"                writel(MXS_I2C_CTRL0_SFTRST,"},{"depth":1,"text":"                                i2c->regs + MXS_I2C_CTRL0_SET);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+               dma_release_channel(i2c->dmach);"},{"depth":1,"text":"                return err;"},{"depth":1,"text":"        }"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"--"},{"depth":1,"text":"2.51.0"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":""}],"lineCount":17,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com","parentId":"20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com"}},"rootIds":["20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com"],"childrenByParent":{"20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com":["an8ntm6GRhFJnrqZ@SMW015318"]},"chronologicalIds":["20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com","an8ntm6GRhFJnrqZ@SMW015318"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{"patch:20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com:0:0":{"id":"patch:20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com:0:0","messageId":"20260814134033.1386874-1-ruoyuw560@gmail.com","subject":"[PATCH] i2c: mxs: fix DMA channel leak